From: PTPT52.AI <ptpt52@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: fix AN7563 FE and QDMA hardware limits

AN7563 has two GDM ports, eight physical TX rings, sixteen RX rings,
two QDMA interrupt register groups, one PPE and 512 PPE SRAM entries.
Use those limits instead of accessing EN7581-only GDM, PSE, QDMA and
PPE resources. Do not expose LRO queues outside the AN7563 RX ring range
or allocate the EN7581-only PPE statistics table.

Keep the 32 logical QoS queues separate from the eight physical TX
rings: DSA selects logical queues 24/31, which must remain valid netdev
queues even though their descriptors use rings 0/7.

The limits, interrupt routing and fragment/reassembly destinations
follow the vendor AN7552 QDMA/PPE definitions. Keep the existing
128-byte PSE, copy engine, OQ, CRSN, IFC and multicast VLAN setup;
the vendor AN7552 code supports these facilities too.

This is a resource-layout correction, not a fix for the unresolved
board TX stall. EN7581 and AN7583 retain their existing limits.

Signed-off-by: PTPT52.AI <ptpt52@gmail.com>
